        <p>, kid!' WIDNks W 1 17E-BEATER JUSTLY PUNISHED. Pk,t Kelly' appeared at the Widnes Police Court, t‘b"uay, to support a warrant granted her last week e arrest of her husband, Peter Kelly, who she 40;4.77 brutally assaulted her on the 19th inst. The ito,s."l-ntrix til "1 her • '. who appeared to be suffering great pain t et,ti Injuries, said that on Wednesday afternoon 'truo_sener followed her through the fields in Moor-lane, Nait' her on the head, threw her down, and said, " I 11 55 until I have taken your life." She was afraid net ,ve with him owing to his brutal conduct, and if she had seven children she would not have forgiven :4lat i.e often as she had done. Sergeant Bennet deposed 1111, 11101. Y to the charge prisoner accused his wife of tY with other men, and said what he would do 4'lliso4ll.)efore he left her. Superintendent Keighlev skid .h*sault; had been previously convicted five times for 116.5 e 1.,;111: his wife.—The Chairman said the court would eve te, Illake an example of prisoner, and he would ,t4es, RO to gaol for four months with hard labour. -,114/1 ParrcitAito, Watchmaker and Jeweller. 51, High A mc',Qra.--.Adet. r, At Nleare Row WITH I CADMAN NEAR WIDNES. , 41.11,1:41clutes Police Court on Monday, John Anderson, akii`tv.as charged with being drunk, and further with iNociirlg a cabman named Patrick Culvert. Defendant :a ~:411,,,r, glailty to being drunk, but denied the assault.— ' pri..ci.,,,tu'rsdtated that hut met defendant in Highfield-road. VPth,oo 43' evening. and he asked him to drive him. to ' . h_wrth new st.ition. When he got there he asked .. 1'1'1114", Intleh he would drive him to The Horns for. . he fiut'B, rePlied 2s Defendant agreed to that, but when . 0 the Horn. Horns he refused tepay the fare, and said , ;111,451". only Is. 61. in his pockets. When witness per- Iqecillii Yetting his fare, defendant knocked him down, htotitonllrn• and bit him on the ear.—Thomas Wright, tiVl-15,q BDoke to hearing a row near the Horns, abo