        <p>THE PLUMBERS' REGISTRATION BILL. WITHDRAWAL OF THE MEASURE. • The Grand Committee of the House of Commons (Mr. Stanafeld in the chair) on Tuesday discussed the Plumbers' Registration Bill, and after a lengthened s,Oebate rejected the definition clause as inadequate to cover the scope of the bill. Upon the next clause (the composition ef the council) a prolonged discussion took place. Sir Julian Goldsmid moved that the chairman leave the chair, which means that the bill should be dropped for the session. Sir Francis Powel?, Mr. Walter Long, Mr. Lees Knowles' and Dr. Farquharson pro- tested. It was eventually decided by 17 votes against 12 not, to proceed further with the bill.</p>
